      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "According to literature data, headaches occur in about 40% of preschool children and up to 70% of the children at school age. Most of the headaches, especially in school children, are idiopathic. Symptomatic headaches accompanying a diversity of diseases occur in a small percentage. The idiopathic headaches are the ones in which the pain is not only the main symptom but also the essence of the disease itself. Other idiopathic headaches include: migraine, tension-type headache and Horton headache. The diagnostic and therapeutic problems in idiopathic headaches are discussed."},
